        "basic_text_ihNVpU": {
          "type": "basic_text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><strong>I'll never forget the day I realized my Shopify store was hemorrhaging potential revenue with every visitor.</strong></p><p>I was running a successful e-commerce business, generating six figures annually. But my conversion rate was stuck at 1.2%—far below the industry standard. Visitors would browse my products, add items to cart, then disappear. My cart abandonment rate was crushing at 78%.</p><p>I had tried everything: expensive Shopify apps, custom coding, hiring freelancers, A/B testing tools, different page builders. Some provided minor improvements, but nothing moved the needle significantly.</p><p><strong>This wasn't supposed to happen to someone like me.</strong> I understood e-commerce, I knew marketing principles, yet here I was—an experienced store owner who couldn't break through the conversion barrier.</p><p>Then I discovered the real problem: my theme wasn't built for conversions. It was beautiful, but it wasn't <em>selling</em>.</p>",
            "highlighted_texts": "hemorrhaging potential revenue with every visitor|This wasn't supposed to happen to someone like me",
            "highlight_texts_color": "#fff3cd",
            "image_position": "above",
            "image_width": 100,
            "padding_top": 0,
            "padding_bottom": 0,
            "padding_left": 0,
            "padding_right": 0
          }
        },
